WEBVTT

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:32.720
<b>dore dake no yoru wo koete bokura meguriaeta kono kiseki wo</b>

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:32.720
<b>How many nights passed before this miracle brought us together?</b>

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:41.400
<b>kasaneai  shinjiau kokoro ga hoshiwataru...</b>

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:41.400
<b>Our hearts, overlapping, trusting in one another, fare the stars...</b>

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.710
Take good care...

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:48.910
<b>ashita ga mienakutemo</b>

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:48.910
<b>Never mind we cannot see tomorrow.</b>

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.410
...of our princess.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:01.250
ABOVE THE RIM

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.220
Destroy!

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.540
That ends this match.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.270
Toriena Heavens are good!

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:19.310
Though they lost their first match, they've since won eight straight matches in a row.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.230
Next time, you're going down.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.480
Then we'll see you in three matches.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:32.710
You think he'll be in time?

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.590
He'll come.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.880
When he does, that will be the League's true tipoff.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.780
Good grief. I never thought I'd hitch a ride on a living ship.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.070
A long life's not bad, if you can get it.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:07.490
It's only because the crisis is here now that we were able to open the path to the moon at all.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.990
Long ago in the legends, I wonder what gave people the idea for this.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:19.370
I'm a machinist, not an archaeologist.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.760
Thanks.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.570
How mature.

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:50.230
Friends with the person your crush likes.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.150
What am I thinking?

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.160
Saving Earthdash and the moon, right?

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.380
Dan'll do that.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.950
We've all chosen the tasks we must complete and the paths we must take.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:04.680
What are you going to do?

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.910
Bloodlines and genes...

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.750
There's something that goes utterly beyond nitpicking over that stuff...

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.890
Something I found in basquash.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.320
But now...

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:18.110
Sela...

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:19.840
What's that?

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.810
Aren't you gonna go inside the ship?

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.810
You can't see the moon once you're on it.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.090
So you're looking at it now?

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.060
Pretty much.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:43.960
What?

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:45.480
Rainbow Plaza.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.120
That was a building in my town!

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.740
Really?

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.530
We went there all the time...

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:55.790
We'd shop for clothes or go out to eat or sit in a teashop...

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:00.290
Dad! Mom!

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.770
Go on. It all hangs on this. {she's speaking to the others who went in the ship}{alt tl: It's the moment of truth.}

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.690
Goodness, dear, do try to move faster!

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:13.560
Wait for me, honey!

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.340
Goal!

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:27.660
Iceman Hotty is on a roll, with no signs of letting up!

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.540
But it's no use! He can't fill the gauge!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.450
We're still waiting for the legend's goal!

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.540
Hey, this thing is gonna get us there, right?!

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.230
It better not fall back down from here!

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.090
It doesn't look like we need to worry.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.300
It looks like we're heading straight there.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.700
Straight where?

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.770
You gotta ask?

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.140
That light...

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.670
What's keeping you, Dan?

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.770
We're out of time.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:02.780
What are you dawdling for?

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.730
Mommy, what'll happen to us?

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.370
Hurry up and get here!

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:13.710
What's that?

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.460
It's a ship that shines.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.740
The legend of the starfarers?

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:26.850
Dan's here.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.430
Yes.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:33.060
I'd better go meet him.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.220
Monitor what Yan's doing on the surface.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:56.630
Have the orbital interception system ready for instant deployment in case of an attack from the Kingdom.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.530
Once, the moon had a royal line as well.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:06.510
More accurately, it was a dynasty that ruled both Earthdash and the moon.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:10.680
My older brother ascended to the moon to become its king,

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.020
and I stayed here on the surface.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.700
Our blood... Our dynasty...

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:21.380
Those tore us apart once, and now things have come to this.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:25.350
Maybe this, too, is because of our royal blood...

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.650
Is that truly what you believe?

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:34.060
Father, why did you inherit the kingship?

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.920
Was it <i>not</i> for the sake of this land and its people?

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.440
We relay the voice of the stones to the people.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:42.800
That is our family's power.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.030
I believed that carrying out my duties as king...

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:52.400
...would keep my promise to my brother, and bring happiness to everyone.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.060
Father...

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:00.330
Thank you!

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.930
This is pretty bad.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:13.780
Yeah.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:15.560
Violette, let's hurry!

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:16.410
Yes.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:18.450
Sorry, we'll be right back.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.960
Sorry, Rouge.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.100
No, no. Be careful, okay?

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:24.260
Hang tough, Purple and Yellow!

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:27.700
Thanks, everybody.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:32.000
Dan, Slash, Iceman...

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.650
We'll entrust this city, and its future, to you!

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.310
W-Welcome, DJD.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.320
They're even shrimpier than Dan!

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.980
DJD?

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.730
DJD for Dan JD!

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.200
Welcome, DJD!

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.490
Welcome!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:57.360
DJD, DJD, DJD...

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:04.490
They're glad to see us.

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:05.910
You all fired up now?

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:07.670
For this, I was <i>born</i> fired up. {sz: lol, very loose tl. Lit., "I never intended on being any other way./I intended [being that way] from the start"}

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:08.700
What about you?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.760
Welcome to Mooneyes.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.640
Now I've finally used that moon passport of yours.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:21.530
The Board has registered Team Basquash as an official participant in the Legend League.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:25.400
We'd like you to join the match lineup as soon as you can.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.690
We can't afford to waste time.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.490
It looks like you're right about that.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:36.160
It's too cruel to call this a just reward. {alt phrase: just desserts/justice}

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:41.170
"The Man of Legend Touches Down in Mooneyes."

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:43.460
"A New Development for the Legend League!"

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:45.540
Brother...

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.500
And Oscarman scores!

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:51.180
But the gauge stays stubborn!

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:54.800
The world can't be saved unless someone becomes the legend!

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.350
Will their efforts bear fruit?

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.040
That's what we're hoping for!

00:08:59.040 --> 00:08:59.850
Iceman!

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.360
Destroy!

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:13.150
Game set. Game set.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:16.600
Another match has ended without the legend's reappearance.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:21.510
But the players are putting their very lives on the line in this battle. {lit meaning is, the players are tapping into their life-force to keep playing, and maybe whittling away years of their lives etc.}

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:23.500
Gotcha. {sz: not really a word, so we don't *need* to sub this. Editor decides}

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:29.140
We will now have a three-hour break so the players can rest and have their mechs undergo maintenance.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.410
Enough time for a drink.

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:35.030
That damned Dan JD.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.450
To think he actually made it to the moon.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:40.010
Riding a star-ship, he comes to the moon:

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:43.580
the man who throws the thunderbolt ball.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:45.060
The legend.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:50.440
Free will is what makes a person a person. {alt phrasing: Deciding your own actions is what makes you a person.}

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:54.490
Someone who's gotten on the "legend" train no longer has any will of his own.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:55.980
He's a puppet.

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:01.240
It appears the atmospheric friction has induced a magnetic field.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:05.540
Our hotlines will no longer reach Mooneyes now.

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.350
We don't need them to.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.100
Sorry I took a while, Iceman.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.150
You're late.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:33.820
Elegantly precise.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:38.160
Your re-tuning for the moon is marvelous.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:42.010
{humph sound}You must be the young man in charge of the moon.

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:46.380
How come you're lounging around here at a time like this?

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:48.100
Because it is a time like this.

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:50.710
Where's your grandchild?

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:52.270
Huh?

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:55.720
If you mean Miyuki, she's repairing another Bigfoot.

00:10:56.770 --> 00:11:02.000
What a load of crap, calling them the "Legend League" when you can't even support the players properly.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:05.690
Never sparing a thought for the guys on bottom, like usual.

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:12.860
Now is the time Takeshi's dream might really come true.

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:17.550
You knew my son, kid? {sz: doesn't literally call him "kid," but does address him directly as "omae-san" (you). "Kid" sort of gets the mixture of rough and polite there}

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:26.790
Take care of yourself, Sou.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.710
"Sou"... He...

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:46.480
We were waiting for you.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:48.350
Yeah.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:51.860
You have to become the legend.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:57.740
Right now, the only ones who can play well enough are my team and yours.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:02.050
Don't you need a handicap?

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.460
Maybe.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:11.750
It's unfair that you have to play right after arriving, with no chance to warm up.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:15.880
I'll take you on with just one arm and one leg, how's that sound?

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.420
Sounds good.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:19.970
No handicaps and no holds barred.

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:23.850
I'll hammer you into the ground before you even get over your spacesickness.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:37.360
The damage piles up here, and there on the moon the Legend League plays all alone.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.450
How are conditions outside?

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:42.950
What's the problem?

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.370
Reports are that the crowd is celebrating, sir.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:46.080
What?

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:48.910
They're watching the Legend League and celebrating, sir!

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:56.440
{bg}DAN JD! DAN JD! DAN JD! DAN JD!

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.680
What?!

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.940
You're our only hope!

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:57.250
Dunk Mask!

00:12:57.640 --> 00:13:00.670
Injured and reeling, the players still fight on...

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:04.490
Now before them appears both a powerful ally and a new foe!

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:06.560
That foe is Team Basquash!

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:10.560
Earthdash's top team, led by Dan JD, Dunk Mask!

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:14.440
Now is the time to show us the legend's power!

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:30.280
Challenging Team Basquash is Toriena Heavens, fresh from their string of wins—

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.550
Wait just a moment!

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:36.980
Princess, my older brother was...

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:39.980
He was Ascend, the king of the moon, wasn't he?

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:42.560
I had heard he went missing quite a long time ago...

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:46.260
There was a legendary secret technique passed down within our family,

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:50.320
the secret of using ultinium's power to become young again.

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:51.930
I see, it was real after all.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.000
Big brother...

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.280
The time has come to use that technique.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:08.690
Now is the time to use that secret and revive the thunderbolt's power!

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:19.600
The king... Our king is gone!

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:20.960
King Ascend!

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.400
The power of the royal dynasty...

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.180
Was it him?

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:33.890
You don't mind?

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:35.730
We lose our chance to team up with Dan this way.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:37.840
Dan is strong.

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:38.930
Besides...

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.070
Aren't you curious to see it?

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:44.730
What a person who's been called the Phantom can really do?

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:48.350
Make a giant?

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.920
Biology's not my field.

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:53.240
I'm a mechanical engineer.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:57.380
I don't mean make an enormous artificial human.

00:14:57.380 --> 00:15:00.670
Make a machine as a means for humans to become giants.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:03.280
That's the load of crap kings always spout.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:06.120
It's not just a matter of money.

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:09.140
It also requires an operator with the right potential.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.450
Very good.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:14.020
Test it out to your heart's content, Sou.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:17.100
The king of the moon.

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.410
Did you know, Yan?

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:28.160
Why research into human reinforcement made such leaps and bounds, so long ago?

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.130
Why bring that up now?

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.240
Ultinium-catalyzed activation of the cells...

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.700
A secret and forbidden technique passed down by the royal family.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.940
Thanks to that, we made it possible to reinforce Eclipse.

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:47.640
But in the end, this whole time we may just have been dancing on the palm of one man's hand.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:10.550
Miss Rouge... switch with me.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:14.910
I don't want to admit it, but we can't beat them with me on the team.

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:20.250
I... I'm too weak to support Miss Sela and Mr. Dan.

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:22.560
We need you.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:25.870
You're the one Team Basquash needs.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.280
Alan...

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:32.720
That's right!

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.890
Handsomely said, Alan.

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:35.740
Get out here, Rouge!

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:37.270
Huh?! B-But...

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:41.540
Pulling yourself out of a match for the good of the team is so damn lame, I could never do it.

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:45.160
But that bastard Alan did it. He's incredible.

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:48.150
Alan, you've shown me your guts and I'm not gonna waste it.{more rambling lit tl: Alan, you've shown me what you can do when you're really serious, and I'm not gonna fumble the chance you've given us.}

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:50.900
What are you gonna do, Rouge?

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:53.620
I'm playing.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.250
Thanks, Dan.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.050
Now that everyone's here, there's one more thing.

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:16.300
It's been ticking me off since I first saw it.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:20.020
Don't fucking think you can mess around here!

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:26.510
On the moon or on the ground, how many times do I gotta say it?

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:29.730
You're here to watch a game, not a gauge!

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:34.230
That's how I'm gonna show you the real legend!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.680
Coco, your big brother's gonna pull it off.

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.030
Watch me, okay?

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:51.620
Can't beat that!

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:54.800
The world's about to end, and just listen to you!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.420
Sela?

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.430
He's right. He's right!

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:01.550
Crawly, I'm all right.

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:04.270
I'm the basquasher Sela Miranda!

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:07.770
I'm gonna make the Platinum Hurricane blow through Mooneyes, just watch!

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:11.740
Oh Princess, oh Aurora.

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:14.690
What should I wait for now?

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:19.370
Now that I'm old and powerless, and the stones have abandoned me?

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:21.640
This is the time to walk on our own legs.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:26.000
No one but the royal family can perform our duties.

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:29.590
Speak not to the stones, but to your people.

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:32.790
Stand up and speak out loud in your own voice.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:39.830
Just as does your daughter, Flora, when she fights as Alan Naismith.

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:43.270
Flora...

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.470
Coming through, excuse us!

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:48.690
Bingo!

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:51.020
Ready, guys?

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:54.040
Alan, this is a long way for a beginner to come.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:57.970
You can be proud of yourself. Watch our backs, okay?

00:18:57.970 --> 00:18:59.120
Okay!

00:18:59.120 --> 00:18:59.980
Sela!

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:01.050
What?

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:03.740
When we're done, I'm gonna settle things with you too.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.230
Nothing stops the hurricane until then!

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:07.250
Way ahead of you!

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.350
Rouge!

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:11.380
Don't think you can retire halfway through this time.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:14.010
We're gonna raise enough hell for the two of them too!

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.430
Stick with me till the end!

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:16.340
You don't have to tell me!

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.830
Old man! And Miyuki too, I guess.

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:20.180
What do you mean, you guess?

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.320
Don't take your eyes off us!

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:26.060
We're gonna stun the whole moon with the masterpieces you two made!

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.270
Don't do me any favors.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:31.230
Make my Dad proud too, Dan!

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:32.510
Spanky!

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:33.800
Yeah, Stupid Dan?

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:35.900
I'm gonna let you eat your fill!

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.430
You get a shot at the whole world!

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:39.760
That sounds big! Leave it to me!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.280
Here we go!

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:43.610
Team...

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:46.250
...Basquash!

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:49.030
Prepare to load the Legend Bullet!

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:50.880
You aren't going to watch them through to the end?

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:54.130
The true legend probably wouldn't be stopped by this.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.420
And any legend pampered with mercy or pity is worthy only of my scorn!

00:19:58.210 --> 00:19:59.260
Understood.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.110
Begin loading the Legend Bullet!

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:05.560
Finally this time has come.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:07.390
Let us begin!

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:09.310
The highest and greatest basquash of all!

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:11.230
Tip...

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:13.820
...off!

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:41.090
First, you say hello.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:44.100
Handicapping him wouldn't be enough, would it?

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:45.720
Bring it on!

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.970
I figured he was something special.

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:50.980
Now that's what I'm talking about.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.400
The ball holds peoples feelings

00:20:56.510 --> 00:20:58.560
Peoples feelings rise.

00:20:58.620 --> 00:20:59.490
and,

00:20:59.510 --> 00:21:00.750
and finally

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:02.180
the legend begins.

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:04.630
The last episode: Free!

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:08.030
NEXT TIME

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:07.790
The people stand and fight.
